## PRE-EXISTING content-accuracy finding (not a WS5 regression, OBSERVATION)
Setting the malformed start date "20266-09" (a five-digit year, the same
class of value this task's own message correctly labels "invalid") makes
the un-related, pre-existing client-side `computeDerivedAge`/
`updatePersonAgePreviews` (web/static/js/whatif-rate-assumptions.js lines
31-51, confirmed BYTE-IDENTICAL to master and untouched by any WS5 attempt
1-4 -- the diff's earliest hunk starts at line 19's
`updatePersonRole`/`removePersonRow`, well past this function) display
"Age 18307" / "Age 18295" in the Derived Age badges instead of a sane
value or "Age -". This is a pre-existing content-accuracy bug (present on
master, reachable via any malformed start date regardless of this task),
not an a11y-specific defect and not introduced by WS5 -- flagged as an
OBSERVATION for the backlog, consistent with the scope rule (git diff
master governs; a hit on markup/JS byte-identical to master is
PRE-EXISTING). It is the likely cause of axe's 2 extra "incomplete"
color-contrast nodes in that one state (same bg/fg colors as baseline;
axe's heuristic reacting to the longer digit string, not a real contrast
regression).

