## Summary
Attempt 4 changed only handlers_rates.go's persons-error classifier (split
into two anchored regexes distinguishing "unparseable" from "after start
date") and its tests -- rate-assumptions.html, whatif-rate-assumptions.js,
and handlers.go are byte-identical to attempt 3 (already PASSed). Live-
traced in both themes: the new unparseable-birth-month message and the
invalid-projection-start-date message are each announced exactly once via
role=alert, sit as the settings form's first child, are truthful (correct
per-shape wording, never conflated), render with real apostrophes/quotes
(wire text is correctly entity-encoded; live DOM/AT-exposed text is not),
pass contrast (5.72:1 light / 8.88:1 dark), and leave focus on the edited
field. The distinct "after start date" message was re-verified unregressed
by the regex split, and a same-field sequential-edit test confirmed no
alert stacking/duplicate announcement across error-class transitions. Glide
checkbox behavior and the linked-removal refusal are unchanged and re-
verified in both themes. axe-core (card expanded, 5 states, both themes)
found 0 new violations; the one dark-mode violation is the same
pre-existing, out-of-scope node attempts 2/3 recorded. One pre-existing,
out-of-scope content-accuracy bug (derived-age display on a malformed start
date) is noted as an OBSERVATION, not a FAIL, per the git-diff-master scope
